==English==
[[Image:Tsetse_head-proboscis.jpeg|thumb|Head of a '''tsetse'''.]]

===Alternative forms===
* [[tzetze]]
* [[tsetze]]

===Etymology===
From the [[Tswana]] {{term|tsêtsê}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pl2=tsetse}}

# {{insect}} Any [[fly]] of the [[genus]] ''[[Glossina]]'', native to [[Africa]], that feeds on human and animal blood; known primarily as a carrier of parasitic [[trypanosome]]s.

====Translations====
{{trans-top|fly of the genus Glossina}}
* Albanian: {{t+|sq|cece|xs=Albanian}}
* German: [[Tsetsefliege]] {{f}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Korean: [[체체파리]] (chechepari)
{{trans-bottom}}

====Usage notes====
* Particularly in North American English, this insect is most commonly referred to as a "tsetse fly."

